---
import Layout from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Games with Grams Privacy Policy"
	description="Privacy Policy for Games with Grams, the turn-based family word game for iPhone and iPad"
	pubDate={new Date('November 15 2026')}
>
	<h2>Privacy Policy for Games with Grams</h2>
	<p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> November 15, 2026</p>

	<h3>Overview</h3>
	<p>
		Games with Grams ("we", "our", or "us") is a turn-based word game for iPhone and iPad with
		built-in chat between the people playing. To make multiplayer games, chat, and turn
		notifications work, the app stores a small amount of information on our servers. This
		policy explains what that is, why we need it, and how you can have it removed.
	</p>
	<p>
		We do not show ads, we do not use analytics or advertising identifiers, we do not track you
		across other apps or websites, and we never sell data.
	</p>

	<h3>Information We Collect</h3>
	<p>
		Everything below is used only to make the app work and is linked to your player profile.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Player identifiers.</strong> When you sign in with Game Center, the app creates an
			account on our servers and stores an account ID together with your Game Center player ID,
			so that the people you play can be matched to their chat conversations with you.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Display name.</strong> Your Game Center display name, so opponents can see who
			they are playing.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Preferences and sign-in times.</strong> Your in-app settings (text size, contrast,
			and sound) and the dates your profile was created and last signed in.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Push notification token.</strong> If you allow notifications, a token that
			identifies the app on your device so we can tell you when it is your turn or when you
			have a new message.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Chat messages and reactions.</strong> The messages and emoji reactions you send to
			the people you play, along with when they were sent and whether they have been read.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Gameplay summaries.</strong> Move summaries that appear in the chat, such as the
			words played, the points scored, and game results.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We do not ask for your real name, email address, phone number, location, contacts, photos,
		microphone, or camera.
	</p>

	<h3>Game Center</h3>
	<p>
		Sign-in, friend invitations, and the matches themselves (the board, tiles, scores, and whose
		turn it is) are handled by Apple's Game Center. If you grant access to your Game Center
		friends list, it is used only on your device to let you choose who to invite; we do not
		store your friends list. Game Center data is held by Apple under Apple's privacy policy and
		can be managed in Settings &gt; Game Center.
	</p>

	<h3>Who Can See Your Information</h3>
	<p>
		Your display name, your chat messages and reactions, and your moves are visible to the
		people you are playing with. They are not public and are not shown to other players.
	</p>

	<h3>Crash Reports</h3>
	<p>
		If the app crashes, a diagnostic report may be sent through Firebase Crashlytics so we can
		find and fix the problem. A report contains technical details such as the device model,
		operating system version, app version, and what the app was doing when it crashed, tied to a
		random installation ID. It does not include your chat messages.
	</p>

	<h3>Data Stored on Your Device</h3>
	<p>
		Your theme choice and chat display preferences are stored locally on your device and are
		removed when you delete the app.
	</p>

	<h3>Third-Party Services</h3>
	<p>
		Our servers are provided by Google Firebase (Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Cloud
		Messaging, and Crashlytics), and push notifications are delivered through Apple. Google and
		Apple process data on our behalf in order to provide these services, and their handling of
		data is governed by their own privacy policies:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy">Firebase Privacy and Security</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
		<li><a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple Privacy Policy</a></li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We do not share your information with anyone else.
	</p>

	<h3>Retention and Deletion</h3>
	<p>
		We keep your profile and chat history for as long as you use the app so that your games and
		conversations are there when you come back. You can ask us to delete your profile and the
		chat messages you sent at any time by emailing the address below with your Game Center
		display name. Turning off notifications for the app in Settings stops new notifications from
		being delivered, and deleting the app removes everything stored on the device.
	</p>

	<h3>Children's Privacy</h3>
	<p>
		Games with Grams is designed for families to play together. We do not ask children for
		personal information beyond what is described above, and we do not show ads or track
		anyone. Game Center accounts for children are managed through Apple's Family Sharing and
		parental controls, which is where a parent can limit multiplayer games and friend requests.
		If you are a parent or guardian and would like your child's profile and messages removed,
		contact us and we will delete them.
	</p>

	<h3>App Store Information</h3>
	<p>
		When you download Games with Grams from the App Store, Apple may collect information
		according to its own privacy policy. We do not receive personally identifiable information
		from Apple beyond the aggregated, anonymous download and crash statistics provided to all
		developers.
	</p>

	<h3>Changes to This Policy</h3>
	<p>
		We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on this
		page with an updated "Last Updated" date.
	</p>

	<h3>Contact Us</h3>
	<p>
		If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, or want your data deleted, please
		contact us at:
	</p>
	<p>
		<a href="mailto:evan+gameswithgrams@mightystrong.io">evan+gameswithgrams@mightystrong.io</a>
	</p>
</Layout>
